# Console Prototype Lab — Agent Rules

This repo is a **shared design playground**, not production Aiven Console.

## Hard rules

- Never use production APIs or real customer data
- Never add secrets, tokens, or private customer information
- Never use production API dependencies
- Optimize for prototype clarity, not production quality

## Edit scope

- **Do not edit** shared reusable scenarios in `src/registry/scenarios.ts` or their runtime unless explicitly requested
- For new design explorations, copy a template into `experiments/<owner>/<name>/`
- **Default edit scope:** only the experiment folder
- Ask before changing shared shell, global mock data structure, `scenarioRuntime` base configs, or shared app components in `src/`

## Reuse first (experiments)

- Reuse domain UI, data, and assets from `experiments/_shared/` before creating new code in an experiment folder
- If a needed dependency is not in `_shared`, copy it from `src/` into `_shared` first, then import from `@experiments/_shared/...`
- Keep the **app-shell contract** on `@/`: `@/contexts/PlaygroundStateContext`, `@/theme/ThemeProvider`, `@/components/experiments/ExperimentPageShell`, `@/lib/experiments/types`
- `_shared` is duplicated from `src/` and must be kept in sync manually when domain code changes

## Reuse first (app)

- Reuse `src/mocks/`, `src/screens/`, `src/components/` before creating new code in the app shell
- Keep code simple and readable

## Creating experiments

```bash
node scripts/create-experiment.mjs --owner <name> --name <slug> --template <templateSlug>
```

Example:

```txt
Use the "Onboarding starter" template as the base.
Create a new experiment under experiments/<your-name>/<experiment-name>/.
Entry file is index.tsx. Modify only that experiment folder.
```

## Discovery

- Experiments and templates are discovered from the filesystem via `src/lib/experiments/discover.server.ts`
- Do not hardcode experiment lists elsewhere

## Deployment

- Deploy via Aiven Application (Product app runtime), port 8080
- No Vercel configuration in this project
